    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d475-a1">

                <pb facs="0501" n="481" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg481"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 1.</seg></opener>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>The Gorogio to Mr. Pruyn</head>
                <p>We have to inform you that, having instructed Sibata Sadataro, governor for
                    foreign affairs, to negotiate with you about the reduction of duties, we
                    carefully read the convention made. We approve it, and shall keep it
                    forever.</p>
                <p>Stated with respect and esteem.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><date calendar="gregorian japanese-nengō"
                            when="1864-01-31">The 23d day of the 12th month of the 3d year of
                            Bunkiu, (January 31, 1864</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>MIDSUMO IDSUMI-NO-KAMI.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>ITAKURA SUWO-NO-KAMI.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>INOWUYE KAWATSI-NO-KAMI.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert H. Pruyn</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the United States of America,
                            &amp;c., &amp;c.,&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
